  "title": "Erdős Problem #468",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For any $n$ let $D_n$ be the set of sums of the shape $d_1,d_1+d_2,d_1+d_2+d_3,\\ldots$ where $1<d_1<d_2<\\cdots$ are the divisors of $n$.\nWhat is the size of $D_n\\backslash \\cup_{m<n}D_m$?\nIf $f(N)$ is the minimal $n$ such that $N\\in D_n$ then is it true that $f(N)=o(N)$? Perhaps just for almost all $N$?\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"L1\"\n},{",
